t bears her name. She was a Jewess named Hadas’sah (the myrtle), but when she entered the royal harem she received the name by which she henceforth became known (Esther 2:7).","verses":46,"father":"Abihail","mother":"","v":[1,2,3,5,6,7,8]},{"id":"haman_1360","name":"Haman","also":"","summary":"(of Persian origin), magnificent, the name of the vizier (i.e., the prime minister) of the Persian king Ahasuerus (Esther 3:1, etc.). He is called an “Agagite,” which seems to denote that he was descended from the royal family of the Amalekites, the bitterest enemies of the Jews, as Agag was one of the titles of the Amalekite kings.","verses":45,"father":"Hammedatha","mother":"","v":[1,6,7,8,9,10]},{"id":"ahasuerus_117","name":"Ahasuerus","also":"","summary":"The son of Darius Hystaspes, the king named in the Book of Esther. He ruled over the kingdoms of Persia, Media, and Babylonia, “from India to Ethiopia.”","verses":29,"father":"","mother":"","v":[5]},{"id":"mordecai_2107","name":"Mordecai","also":"","summary":"The son of Jair, of the tribe of Benjamin. It has been alleged that he was carried into captivity with Jeconiah, and hence that he must have been at least one hundred and twenty-nine years old in the twelfth year of Ahasuerus (Xerxes).","verses":50,"father":"Jair","mother":"","v":[9,10]},{"id":"harbonah_1411","name":"Harbonah","also":"","summary":"","verses":1,"father":"","mother":"","v":[9]}],"places":[],"events":[],"traditions":[],"sources":["JFB","MHCC","Wesley"],"tags":{"bsb":[[4428,4428,4428,2001,2001,935,8354,8354,5973,635,4436,4436],[4960,4960,4960,4960,3196,3196,8145,8145,8145,3117,4428,4428,559,1571,1571,4436,635,4100,4100,7596,7596,5414,5414,5414,5414,0,0,4100,4100,1246,1246,5704,5704,5704,2677,4438,4438,6213,6213,6213,6213],[4436,635,6030,518,4672,4672,4672,2580,5869,5869,5869,4428,4428,518,518,2896,2896,4428,4428,5414,0,5315,5315,7596,7596,7596,5971,5971,5971,5971,5971,5971,1246,1246,1246],[3588,5971,5971,589,589,4376,4376,4376,4376,8045,8045,2026,6,6,432